Package: longlineTypology
Title: Clustering Analysis for Longline Fisheries Data
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Romain", "Forestier", , "romainf@spc.int", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements a k-means clustering method to develop a typology
    of heterogeneous longline fishing practices, aggregating fisheries
    data into distinct groups based on shared technical and operational
    characteristics. Designed to accept fisheries catch-effort and
    length-frequency data in the format produced by the 'seafisheries'
    package, though any correctly formatted fisheries data can be used.
    The clustering method is described in the manuscript,
    "A comprehensive method to integrate fisheries data in
    spatially-explicit population dynamics models". This is a base-R build:
    functionally identical to the upstream package but with the dplyr, rlang
    and factoextra dependencies removed. See BASE-R-CHANGES.md.
